research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-3691-**Given:** The space $\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{N}}$, the subset $V$, the functions $N_1$ and $N_\infty$ above, and, for $m \ge 1$, the vector $u^{(m)} \in V$ with $u^{(m)}_j = 1$ for $j<m$ and $u^{(m)}_j = 0$ for $j \ge m$. For $i \in \mathbb{N}$, $e_i \in \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{N}}$ is the function with $e_i(i) = 1$ and $e_i(j) = 0$ for $j \ne i$.
