research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-3695-[L1] $\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{N}}$ is a vector space over $\mathbb{R}$ with pointwise operations, and a nonempty $W$ with $\lambda u + w \in W$ for all $\lambda$ and all $u,w \in W$ is a linear subspace, hence itself a vector space ([[def-function-space]], [[def-vector-space]], [[def-linear-subspace]], [[lem-linear-subspace-criterion]]).
