research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log:4090:[L3] Heine-Borel in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ for $n \ge 1$: a subset of $(\mathbb{R}^{n},d_2)$ is compact if and only if it is closed and bounded ([[thm-heine-borel-rn]] clause 2, [[def-metric-compactness]], [[def-metric-topology]], [[def-metric-bounded-diameter]]).
