research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-4125-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log:4126:4.1 By the extreme value theorem applied to the nonempty compact metric space $(S,d_S)$ and the continuous $N|_S$, there is $x_{\min} \in S$ with $N(x_{\min}) \le N(x)$ for every $x \in S$; put $c := N(x_{\min})$. [step 1.4, step 1.5, step 3.1, L4]
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-4127-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log-4128-5.1 $c > 0$: from $x_{\min} \in S$ we get $\lVert x_{\min}\rVert_2 = 1 \ne 0$, so $x_{\min} \ne 0$ by (N1) for $\lVert\cdot\rVert_2$, so $N(x_{\min}) \ne 0$ by (N1) for $N$, and $N(x_{\min}) \ge 0$; trichotomy leaves $c > 0$. [step 4.1, L7, L9]
