research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-page-rn-as-a-normed-space.log:5734: - **Where the proof of [[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]] breaks on $V$.** That proof takes the unit sphere of $\lVert\cdot\rVert_2$, which is closed and bounded, and concludes compactness from [[thm-heine-borel-rn]] — a theorem about $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ for a natural $n$, proved by bisecting finitely many coordinates. On $V$ there is no such theorem, and indeed [[fs-heine-borel-holds-in-every-normed-space]] refutes the corresponding claim on the same space.
