research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4389-research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-fs-the-rearrangement-sums-of-a-non-absolutely-convergent-series-fill-the-space-r2.log:11439:[L6] The inner product, the Euclidean norm and the definition of $\Gamma$ and $\Gamma^{\perp}$ ([[def-euclidean-inner-product]], [[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[def-norm-and-normed-space]], [[def-the-space-of-summing-directions]], [[thm-of-square-roots]], [[def-integer-power]]).
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4390-research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-fs-the-rearrangement-sums-of-a-non-absolutely-convergent-series-fill-the-space-r2.log:11477:- **What the example makes concrete.** $\Gamma$ is computed from its definition, one direction at a time, and turns out to be the set of directions orthogonal to where the series actually moves: testing against $e_1$ sees only zeros, and testing against $e_0$ sees the alternating harmonic series, which is not absolutely summable. That is exactly the dichotomy [[def-the-space-of-summing-directions]] is built to record.
