research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4897-**Equivalence of norms.** [[def-equivalent-norms]] defines equivalence and proves
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4898-the dictionary: equivalent norms give **Lipschitz** equivalent metrics, the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4899-strongest of the three tiers of [[def-equivalent-metrics]] and
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4900-[[thm-metric-equivalence-hierarchy]], hence the same open sets, convergent
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4901-sequences, Cauchy sequences and uniformly continuous maps.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4902-[[lem-every-norm-on-rn-is-continuous-for-the-euclidean-metric]] does the half
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4903-that costs no compactness: the finite and reverse triangle inequalities for any
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4904-norm, the bound $N(x) \le C\lVert x\rVert_1$ from the standard basis, the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4905-comparison chain
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4906-$\lVert x\rVert_\infty \le \lVert x\rVert_2 \le \lVert x\rVert_1 \le \iota(n)\lVert x\rVert_\infty$,
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4907-and Lipschitz continuity of $N$ for $d_2$.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log:4908:[[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]] supplies the other half by compactness of
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4909-the Euclidean unit sphere, through [[thm-heine-borel-rn]] and
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4910-[[thm-extreme-value-metric]]; the hypothesis $n \ge 1$ is used twice there and
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-4911-both uses are marked.
