research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7250-### Absolute convergence
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7251-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7252-$\sum x_k$ **converges absolutely** when the real series
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7253-$\sum \lVert x_k\rVert_2$ converges ([[def-series]]); since
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7254-$\lVert x_k\rVert_2 \ge 0$ ([[def-norm-and-normed-space]]), this is a statement
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7255-about a series of nonnegative terms, exactly as in
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7256-[[def-absolute-and-conditional-convergence]].
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7257-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7258-**The choice of norm is immaterial.** If $N$ is any norm on $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ then
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7259-$c\lVert x_k\rVert_2 \le N(x_k) \le C\lVert x_k\rVert_2$ for fixed $c, C > 0$
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log:7260:([[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]], [[def-equivalent-norms]]), so
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7261-$\sum N(x_k)$ converges exactly when $\sum\lVert x_k\rVert_2$ does, both being
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7262-series of nonnegative terms. The notion defined above therefore depends on
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7263-$\mathbb{R}^{n}$ and not on the norm chosen to test it.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7264-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7265-### Rearrangement and the set of rearrangement sums
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7266-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7267-Let $\sigma : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ be a bijection
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7268-([[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]). The **rearrangement of $\sum x_k$ along
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7269-$\sigma$** is the series $\sum x_{\sigma(k)}$ of the sequence
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7270-$k \mapsto x_{\sigma(k)}$, verbatim as in
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7271-[[def-rearrangement-and-unconditional-convergence]] one dimension down. The
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-7272-**set of rearrangement sums** of $(x_k)$ is
--
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8732-2.2 $\sum_{k<n}x_k^{2} = \sum_{k<n}|x_k|\,|x_k| \le \sum_{k<n}|x_k|\,\lVert x\rVert_1 = \lVert x\rVert_1\sum_{k<n}|x_k| = \lVert x\rVert_1^{2}$, using step 1.4 termwise, monotonicity and scaling; taking nonnegative square roots gives $\lVert x\rVert_2 \le \lVert x\rVert_1$. [step 1.4, L4, L7, L9, L10]
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8733-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8734-2.3 Applying step 1.1 to the list $i \mapsto x_i e_i$ and then (N2): $N(x) = N\bigl(\sum_{i<n}x_ie_i\bigr) \le \sum_{i<n}N(x_ie_i) = \sum_{i<n}|x_i|\,N(e_i) \le \sum_{i<n}|x_i|\,C = C\lVert x\rVert_1$, the last inequality by monotonicity from step 1.7. This is clause 2. [step 1.1, step 1.7, step 1.8, L1, L4, L7]
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8735-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8736-3.1 Steps 2.1, 2.2, 1.5 and 1.6 are the four inequalities of clause 3; since $\iota(n) > 0$ and $\sqrt{\iota(n)} > 0$, they exhibit positive constants in both directions for each of the three pairs, so the three norms are pairwise equivalent. [step 1.5, step 1.6, step 2.1, step 2.2, L11, L9]
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8737-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8738-3.2 By step 1.2 applied on $\mathbb{R}^{n}$, then step 2.3, then step 1.6: $\bigl|N(x)-N(y)\bigr| \le N(x-y) \le C\lVert x-y\rVert_1 \le C\sqrt{\iota(n)}\;\lVert x-y\rVert_2$. [step 1.2, step 1.6, step 2.3, L4]
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8739-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-def-the-space-of-summing-directions.log-8740-4.1 Since $\lVert x-y\rVert_2 = d_2(x,y)$ and $\bigl|N(x)-N(y)\bigr| = d_{\mathbb{R}}(N(x),N(y))$, step 3.2 says exactly that $N$ is Lipschitz with the nonnegative constant $C\sqrt{\iota(n)}$, hence uniformly continuous and continuous; this is clause 4, and with steps 1.2, 2.3 and 3.1 all four clauses are proved. [step 1.2, step 2.3, step 3.1, step 3.2, L7, L12] ∎
