research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2085-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2086-- **Why the intrinsic derivative is stated first.** The componentwise formula is
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2087-  the one used in computations, but it is tied to the standard basis, whereas the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2088-  limit of the difference quotient is not. The intrinsic form is the one that
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2089-  survives when the domain is enlarged from an interval to a subset of
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2090-  $\mathbb{R}^{n}$, which is a later page of this track.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2091-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2092-- **No norm appears in either definition.** The derivative is a limit in
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log:2093:  $(\mathbb{R}^{m}, d_2)$, and by [[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]] the same
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2094-  limits are obtained from any other norm, so the notion does not depend on the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2095-  choice ([[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]). The integral
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2096-  is defined coordinatewise and mentions no metric at all.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2097-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2098-- **Integrability of $\lVert f\rVert_2$ is a separate matter** and is not part of
