research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2814-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2815-**Given:** A natural $n \ge 1$; the space $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ with the norms of [[def-p-norms-on-rn]] and the metric $d_2$; a sequence $\bigl(x^{(j)}\bigr)$ in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$; a point $x \in \mathbb{R}^{n}$; a norm $N$ on $\mathbb{R}^{n}$; and a rational $\varepsilon > 0$.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2816-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-2817-[L1] The comparison chain for $n \ge 1$ ([[lem-every-norm-on-rn-is-continuous-for-the-euclidean-metric]] clause 3): $\lVert y\rVert_\infty \le \lVert y\rVert_2 \le \lVert y\rVert_1 \le \iota(n)\lVert y\rVert_\infty$ for every $y \in \mathbb{R}^{n}$, where $\lVert y\rVert_\infty = \max\{|y_k| : k<n\}$ ([[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[lem-finite-set-has-max]], [[def-max-min]]).
