research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5144-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5145-- **Why the intrinsic derivative is stated first.** The componentwise formula is
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5146-  the one used in computations, but it is tied to the standard basis, whereas the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5147-  limit of the difference quotient is not. The intrinsic form is the one that
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5148-  survives when the domain is enlarged from an interval to a subset of
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5149-  $\mathbb{R}^{n}$, which is a later page of this track.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5150-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5151-- **No norm appears in either definition.** The derivative is a limit in
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log:5152:  $(\mathbb{R}^{m}, d_2)$, and by [[thm-all-norms-on-rn-are-equivalent]] the same
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5153-  limits are obtained from any other norm, so the notion does not depend on the
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5154-  choice ([[def-p-norms-on-rn]], [[def-euclidean-inner-product]]). The integral
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5155-  is defined coordinatewise and mentions no metric at all.
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5156-
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5157-- **Integrability of $\lVert f\rVert_2$ is a separate matter** and is not part of
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5158-  this definition: it is proved, together with the inequality it belongs to, in
research/audit/wave12-A9-dispatch/certifier-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed.log-5159-  [[thm-norm-inequality-for-the-vector-valued-integral]].
